  "definition": "t_high = clk rise to dataout valid (50% crossing, 5 fF, 20 ps slew, worst polarity); t_low = clk fall to both addressed bitlines restored to >= 90% VDD (worst over the read table); the candidate period t_high + t_low is then re-simulated (stage A + stage B, both polarities, two cycles with the column mux switching between them): pass = cycle-2 dataout correct and cycle-1 bitlines restored before the cycle-2 rise.  min_period = 1.2 x the verified period.  The wordline and precharge are level-controlled by clk in this design (measured: they retire after the clock falls), so the period is a high-phase plus a low-phase requirement, not a single self-timed chain.",
