 "setup_hold_method": "stage A, one cycle (clk high 0.5 to 1.1 ns), input edges 20 ps; bisection (5 iterations) on the input's 50% crossing relative to the clk 50% rise.  Each scenario first runs its own REFERENCE (the new value held stable) and records the clk-to-edge of the watched control nets (reference_ps).  Setup: the input switches to the new value at t (negative = before the edge) and PASSES if the watched edges come no later than the reference plus 10 ps, the quiet nets (the wrong wordline) stay below 10% VDD, and for the mux bit the column selects are settled when sae fires.  Hold: the input holds the new value through the edge and switches away at t (positive = after the edge); PASS = same criterion.  setup_ps = -(latest passing arrival); hold_ps = earliest passing departure; the measured edges of every bisection point are kept in search[]. Resolution = bracket / 2^iterations.",
 "wd_method": "stage A two-cycle write (cycle 1: read=0, byte_wrenab=1) then read (cycle 2) waveforms drive stage B; the addressed cell is preset to the complement of wd; PASS = the cell's bitline-side node is at wd before the readback edge AND cycle-2 dataout returns wd.  wd's 50% crossing is bisected relative to the cycle-1 clk rise, same brackets and iteration count as the stage A inputs.",
